steps.diagnosis_json:
{
  "spec_element": "invariant",
  "proof_obligation": "preservation",
  "diagnosis": "The loop invariant `forall i :: 1 <= i < n - 1 ==> a[i] == old(a[i-1])` is too weak by one. During an iteration, after n is incremented, the invariant must hold for all i < n; however before the body it only covers i < n-1. In particular, for i == n-1 after the increment the needed fact is missing, so the invariant cannot be proved maintained. The same off-by-one means that at loop exit (n == a.Length) the invariant covers only i < a.Length-1, leaving the postcondition for i == a.Length-1 unproved (bridge)."
}

